      "gap": "The proof of thm:p15-huber-general-minimax does not write out the consistency argument for the midpoint convex M-estimator on the centred class C_k^0: it says only that 'the score sign implications and the strong law for the bounded score give consistency, as in the convex-estimator proof in thm:p15-convex-location-normality' (handbook/annex/p15/huber-information-game.tex lines 581-584). It also reaches the all-equivariant minimax conclusion with 'Taking the exact ordered limits establishes the all-equivariant minimax assertion' (lines 641-642) without writing the limit step. The entry must supply, in full, the consistency proof (signs of lambda_F at +t and -t, the strong law for the bounded score, and T_n -> 0) and the ordered-limit step that combines the pointwise limiting truncated-risk upper bound 1/I_* with the integrated-score lower bound, so that the exact statistical interpretation is fully argued.",
